  {
   "k": "a8l2b4",
   "en": "At the start of HOI4 in 1936 Venezuela is under the rule of President Eleazar López Contreras who was a former general under the previous dictator who had died in 1935. During these initial years of President Contreras rule, his focus was using the authoritarian system of government he inherited to force through new bills to develop the infrastructure of the nation as well as drafting a new constitution which would both start a process of Democratization of the government but also ban Communism in the country. Once World War Two started in 1939, Venezuela's primary focus became the protection of its oil industry from possible sabotage and to exploit the need for oil to increase its economy. Due to the fact the nation declared its neutrality in 1939 it became a notable nation in regards to its role to continue to sell oil to ⟦0⟧, ⟦1⟧, and ⟦2⟧. It was this very reason however that also drew the attention of The ⟦3⟧ who would impose a blockade which caused all trade to Germany to cease. During this economic boom while Venezuela would sell oil to both the ⟦4⟧ and Allies, the nation would take the opportunity to finance the modernization of its military by purchasing aircraft from the ⟦5⟧ and vessels for its navy from ⟦6⟧. Under intense pressure from the Allies, Venezuela would break off relations with the Axis in 1941 after which several Venezuelan freighters would be sunk by U-boats in the Caribbean. In addition Venezuela would grant the Allies full access to its airfields and harbors in order to patrol against further U-boat attacks.",
